      "id": "s2",
      "concept": "Electrochemical theory of corrosion",
      "narration": "In wet corrosion, metal surfaces react with water and oxygen. Iron acts as an anode, releasing electrons and forming Fe^2⁺ ions. These reactions occur in an electrochemical cell where iron is oxidized and oxygen is reduced.",
