      "id": "s6",
      "concept": "Protection methods: Sacrificial anode",
      "narration": "Sacrificial anodes, like zinc, are attached to metal surfaces to corrode instead of the protected metal. Zinc has a lower potential than iron and corrodes preferentially, protecting iron structures.",
